    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0327" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/940: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-16">October 16,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>964. Reference Embassy’s telegram 1160, October 12. Please transmit the following
                    message from the President to Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I deeply appreciate your warm and generous message regarding the step
                            which the Government of the United States has taken in reference to
                            extraterritoriality. That step is one which this Government and I
                            personally have long wished to take, and it is especially gratifying
                            that it could be synchronized with so auspicious a day as China’s
                            national anniversary when your country celebrates the founding of the
                            Republic and honors the principles of freedom. We greatly admire the
                            telling blows for freedom which China has struck against the aggressor
                            in Asia, and we are wholly confident that our two countries in
                            association with our other comrades-in-arms will move forward together
                            to complete victory. Franklin D. Roosevelt”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
